RefDataFieldReference.description:
A reference to another field on the same instrument, used for
field-to-field comparisons. Instead of comparing a field against a
static value, this allows comparing one field against another.

For example, to ensure that `days_to_next_sink` is greater than
`call_notification_min`:

```json
{
  "days_to_next_sink": {
    "greater_than": { "$field": "call_notification_min" }
  }
}
```

RefDataFilter.description:
A `RefDataFilter` is an expression that is used to identify a set of
instruments based on their ref data characteristics.

A simple expression is a reference data field name, an operator and one
or more operands. E.g. the expression

```json
{
  "type": {
    "in": [ "treasury" ]
  }
}
```

would select all instruments that have a `type` attribute with the value of
`treasury`.

A `RefDataFilter` can also be a compound expression. There are 2 flavors,
an `and` expression and an `or` expression. Both are arrays of
`RefDataFilter`s. E.g.

```json
{
  "and": [
    {
      "type": {
        "in": [ "treasury" ]
      }
    },
    {
      "currency": {
        "equal_to": "USD"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

